## Previously raised findings (review-round registry)

These defects were raised on earlier review rounds of this PR. For each finding below: verify fixed (cite the fixing hunk), withdraw (reason required), or mark re-introduced. New claims need new evidence — a claim already on this list is answered, not re-raised.

| id | status | severity | file | claim |
|----|--------|----------|------|-------|
| F1 | open | IMPORTANT | lib/src/cli/provider_error_text.dart | ⚠️ important hour scale retry after hints render as seconds — a wrong time claim retryafterpattern provider error text dart 116 knows only s sec seconds m min minutes for an hour shaped hint the d captures the number the unit group fails to match unit is null — and the render at 164 168 appends s text 429 daily quota reached try again in 23h → …— retry after 23s rate limited retry after 1h → …— retry after 1s verified by running the exact regex render ternary from this diff try again in 23h → retry after 23s off by 3600× retry after 1h → retry after 1s this contradicts the border case principle the pr itself pins one comment above the regex provider error text dart 112 115 absent hint no time claim issue 2119 border case — the ac2 test asserts isnot contains retry after precisely so the line never claims a wrong time hour wordings are a real provider shape for daily 24h quota windows try again in 23h and the rate limit guard set quota resource 0 30 exhausted b429 b routes them into this branch a user told 23s retries immediately and burns exactly the quota the line warns about fix 2 lines add h hr hours to the unit alternation and render h when the unit starts with h for any unit outside s m h omit the claim entirely keep the no wrong claim behavior dart final regexp retryafterpattern regexp r retry after try again in s d s h hr hours s sec seconds m min minutes casesensitive false test to add classifyproviderfailure 429 daily quota reached try again in 23h → contains retry after 23h or for the conservative fix isnot contains retry after retry after 45m stays 45m already correct — keep pinned |

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

